    "body": "DUNCAN_NIGHT_REPORT_R01\nCYCLE_ID = DNR01-20260829-001\nSOURCE_WINDOW = 2026-08-29 / first manual proof cycle\nMAIN_HEAD_OBSERVED = d805242a8ba6e2b169c1216acd3df86b8f9ddd84\nDAY_EVENTS_REVIEWED = issue:204; issue:202; issue:206; Permanent Archive V1 current contract; PR:111 current open/draft bus\n\nTOPICS_STUDIED =\n1. CAMERA_MATH / projective geometry\n2. EDITING_RHYTHM / ordered shot timing\n3. PERSISTENT_IDENTITY / git-backed memory + protected PRIME core\n\nOSS_SOURCES =\n- letta-ai/letta + letta-ai/letta-code + letta-ai/letta-docs-md | Apache-2.0 family | EVALUATE\n- MineDojo/Voyager | MIT | PATTERN_ONLY / curriculum + verified skill library\n- stanfordnlp/dspy / GEPA | MIT | LATER_GATE after real train/validation metrics\n- leanprover-community/mathlib4 | Apache-2.0 | EVALUATE for formal math verification\n- AcademySoftwareFoundation/OpenTimelineIO | Apache-2.0 | ADOPT_FOR_TIMELINE_ANALYSIS_CANDIDATE\n- Breakthrough/PySceneDetect | BSD-3-Clause | EVALUATE_FOR_SHOT_SEGMENTATION\n- isl-org/Open3D | MIT | EVALUATE_FOR_GEOMETRY_LAB\n- colmap/colmap | GPL family | RESEARCH_ONLY_BY_DEFAULT / separate production license review\n\nEXERCISES =\nCAMERA_E01: pinhole camera, image 1920x1080, vertical FOV=60 deg. Computed fy=935.307436 px. Projected P=(0.5,0.2,2.0) -> pixel=(1193.826859,446.469256). Inverse projection at known Z recovered (0.5000000000000002,0.2,2.0).\nEDIT_E01: compared shot-duration vectors A=[6,5,4,3,2,1] and B=[3.5,3.5,3.5,3.5,3.5,3.5]. Both total=21 s, mean=3.5 s, cuts/min=14.285714; A stdev=1.707825 and consecutive delta=[-1,-1,-1,-1,-1], B stdev=0 and delta=[0,0,0,0,0].\nIDENTITY_E01: mapped DUNCAN memory into PRIME_CORE vs editable experience. Letta MemFS upstream states system memory is always in-context; memory is git-backed; dreaming/reflection can update memory; MemFS pre-commit protection rejects edits to protected read_only files. Candidate mapping: PRIME_CORE -> protected read_only system memory; EXPERIENCE/SKILLS -> editable/versioned memory.\n\nVERIFICATION =\n- CAMERA_E01 round-trip numeric error: floating-point only (~2.2e-16 on X); PASS.\n- EDIT_E01 demonstrates identical aggregate cut rate does NOT imply identical rhythm; order/derivative carries information; PASS.\n- IDENTITY_E01 upstream support found for protected read_only memory plus git history; architecture claim PASS AS CANDIDATE, runtime deployment NOT TESTED.\n\nFAILURES =\n- Letta runtime not installed/evaluated on HOME-PC in this cycle.\n- Lean/mathlib executable formal-proof smoke not run in this cycle.\n- Therefore no claim of deployed persistent DUNCAN runtime or formal-math PROVEN skill.\n\nROOT_CAUSES =\n- Prior architecture risk: treating chat/model instance as personality continuity. Durable identity needs external/versioned memory plus runtime enforcement.\n- Prior cinematography-analysis risk: reducing pacing to average shot length/cut rate loses ordered temporal structure.\n- Prior geometry risk: treating screen pixels as body/scene geometry without camera model violates issue #202.\n\nNEW_LEARNING_CANDIDATES =\n1. CAMERA LAW: screen-space delta becomes physically interpretable only after camera/projection is bound; preserve coordinate-space labels through QC.\n2. EDITING LAW: rhythm representation must preserve ordered duration vector and temporal deltas; mean/cuts-per-minute are insufficient summaries.\n3. IDENTITY LAW: PRIME_CORE should be runtime-protected/read_only and separately versioned from editable experience/skills; nightly reflection may learn around the core but must not silently rewrite it.\n\nREGRESSION_RESULTS =\nREUSE_FIRST = PASS. R01 reused #204 + Permanent Archive + PR #111 + native ChatGPT scheduled task; no second archive, scheduler, vector DB, communication bus, or custom agent framework was created.\nSTATE_EVIDENCE_LAW = PASS. Night School was not called RUNNING merely from intent; durable issue #206 and an enabled recurring task exist before this report.\n\nTRANSFER_TEST = PASS / applied `ASSIGNED != RUNNING` evidence discipline to the new learning system: only actual durable contract + actual enabled schedule + actual cycle evidence can satisfy R01 gates.\n\nSKILL_DELTA =\n- projective_camera_reasoning: PARTIAL -> PARTIAL+ / numeric regression verified, formal/general benchmark pending\n- editing_rhythm_analysis: UNTESTED -> PARTIAL\n- persistent_agent_identity_architecture: UNTESTED -> PARTIAL\n- formal_math_with_Lean: UNTESTED\n- letta_runtime_operation: UNTESTED\n\nZORR_APPLICATION =\n- Babylon/camera QC should retain world/view/projection/screen separation and bind camera before pixel-to-geometry conclusions.\n- Future montage analysis should store ordered shot durations/cuts in OTIO-compatible structures and evaluate rhythm beyond aggregate statistics.\n- DUNCAN PRIME candidate should evaluate Letta MemFS with read_only PRIME_CORE and editable/versioned experience/skills before any custom memory system.\n\nPRIME_CORE_CHANGED = NO\nPRODUCTION_MUTATION = NO\nCANON_MUTATION = NO\nSELF_AWARDED_QC_PASS = NO\n\nNEXT_TARGETS =\n1. Isolated Letta Code/MemFS smoke: create protected read_only PRIME_CORE, editable EXPERIENCE, force reflection attempt, prove core cannot change and experience can.\n2. Lean/mathlib minimal theorem smoke relevant to projection/geometry.\n3. OTIO + PySceneDetect real-video/timeline analysis smoke with measured shot sequence.\n4. Build first frozen DUNCAN regression/transfer benchmark set; do not let learner author holdout answers.",
